# Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer's −7: "Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of
# coins that came up heads." Ral is cast on turn 1 and climbs to 7 with four +1s (turns 1, 3, 5, 7; each surveil 2
# keeps the cards on top). On turn 9 the −7 flips heads, tails, heads, heads, tails (the dice: face 1 is heads), so Bot2
# skips its next three turns (CR 500.11, 614.10): the turns that would be Bot2's are proceeded past as though they did
# not exist, and each skipped turn has no number, so Bot1 takes turns 10, 11 and 12 and Bot2's next turn is turn 13. One
# skip is used up by each turn it skips (CR 614.10a). Ral, at 0 loyalty, is put into the graveyard (CR 704.5i).

